WEBVTT

00:42:27.474 --> 00:42:30.903
So to assume we'll have a bunch
more breakthroughs

00:42:30.927 --> 00:42:33.992
and suddenly, AI just becomes
smarter than people --

00:42:34.016 --> 00:42:38.595
there is no engineering path
to get us from here to there.

00:42:38.619 --> 00:42:40.627
CA: Just to push back
on that for a minute.

00:42:40.651 --> 00:42:44.220
Some of the argument from the people
who are so excited about deep learning

00:42:44.244 --> 00:42:46.688
is around the fact
that when you look st the brain,

00:42:46.712 --> 00:42:48.523
the different cognitive functions

00:42:48.547 --> 00:42:50.649
that cover most of the things
we care about

00:42:50.673 --> 00:42:53.474
happen in the same physical infrastructure

00:42:53.498 --> 00:42:59.022
and isn't it possible
that what a child does as they develop

00:42:59.046 --> 00:43:02.625
is a massive series of essentially
deep-learning-type algorithms